WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Picture a country that
makes just two things:

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.170
food and machines.

3
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.620
Its land, workers and tools are limited.

4
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.190
So every new machine
means less food somewhere.

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.400
Economists draw every best
possible mix of the two

6
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.990
as a single curve.

7
00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:21.260
So why does each extra machine
cost more and more food?

8
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.080
In this mission, you'll calculate
opportunity cost from a table,

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.120
then slide along the curve
to test a prediction.

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.900
Then you'll see what
shifts the whole curve,

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.890
from new technology to the
2011 earthquake in Japan.

12
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.470
Your mission: find out why
the curve bows outward,

13
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.400
and what that means for
every choice a country makes.
